<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="text-align: right; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><IMG SRC="alzamendlogo_sm.jpg" ALT="">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 18pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 18pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>Alzamend Neuro Announces Reverse Stock Split</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">ATLANTA, GA, October 30, 2023 -- Alzamend Neuro,
Inc. (Nasdaq: ALZN) (&ldquo;<B>Alzamend</B>&rdquo; or the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;), a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company focused
on developing novel products for the treatment of Alzheimer&rsquo;s disease (&ldquo;<B>Alzheimer&rsquo;s</B>&rdquo;), bipolar disorder
(&ldquo;<B>BD</B>&rdquo;), major depressive disorder (&ldquo;<B>MDD</B>&rdquo;) and post-traumatic stress disorder (&ldquo;<B>PTSD</B>&rdquo;),
today announced that Alzamend&rsquo;s board of directors approved a one-for-fifteen reverse stock split of Alzamend&rsquo;s common stock
(&ldquo;<B>Common Stock</B>&rdquo;) that will be effective in the State of Delaware at 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time on October 31, 2023. Beginning
with the opening of trading on October 31, 2023, the Company&rsquo;s Common Stock will trade on The Nasdaq Capital Market on a split-adjusted
basis under the Company&rsquo;s existing trading symbol &ldquo;ALZN&rdquo;. The new CUSIP number for the Common Stock will be 02262M407.
The reverse stock split is part of the Company&rsquo;s plan to regain compliance with the Minimum Bid Price Requirement of $1.00 per share
required to maintain continued listing on The Nasdaq Capital Market, among other benefits.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in">The reverse stock split affects
all issued and outstanding shares of the Company&rsquo;s Common Stock, as well as the number of shares of Common Stock available for issuance
under the Company&rsquo;s equity incentive plans. In addition, the reverse stock split reduces the number of shares of Common Stock issuable
upon the exercise of stock options or warrants outstanding immediately prior to the reverse split. The par value of the Company&rsquo;s
Common Stock will remain unchanged at $0.0001 per share after the reverse stock split. The reverse stock split affects all stockholders
uniformly and will not alter any stockholder&rsquo;s percentage interest in the Company&rsquo;s equity, except to the extent that the
reverse stock split results in some stockholders owning a fractional share. No fractional shares will be issued in connection with the
reverse split. Stockholders who would otherwise be entitled to receive a fractional share will instead receive a cash payment.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in">Computershare Trust Company,
N.A. (&ldquo;<B>Computershare</B>&rdquo;), is acting as the exchange agent and transfer agent for the reverse stock split. Computershare
will provide instructions to stockholders for receiving payment for any fractional shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>About Alzamend Neuro </B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Alzamend Neuro is a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical
company focused on developing novel products for the treatment of Alzheimer&rsquo;s, BD, MDD and PTSD. Our mission is to rapidly develop
and market safe and effective treatments. Our current pipeline consists of two novel therapeutic drug candidates, AL001 - a patented ionic
cocrystal technology delivering lithium via a therapeutic combination of lithium, salicylate and L-proline, and ALZN002 - a patented method
using a mutant-peptide sensitized cell as a cell-based therapeutic vaccine that seeks to restore the ability of a patient&rsquo;s immunological
system to combat Alzheimer&rsquo;s. Both of our product candidates are licensed from the University of South Florida Research Foundation,
Inc. pursuant to royalty-bearing exclusive worldwide licenses.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B></B></P>

